1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * From [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raziye_Sultan '''Wikipedia'''], the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Raziye Sultan'''[1] (Ottoman Turkish: راضیہ سلطان‎, also known as Tasasız Raziye Sultan[2] (Tasasız meaning "Carefree") was an Ottoman princess, the daughter of Ottoman Sultan Suleiman the Magnificent.[2] She is buried in the Y
2 CONC ahya Efendi Tekkesi in Beshiktash, Istanbul.
2 CONT
2 CONT (the following is translated from her Turkish Wikipedia page)
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Birth''': 1525 Istanbul
2 CONT * '''Death''': 1570/71[citation needed] İstanbul
2 CONT * '''Place of burial''': Yahya Efendi Türbesi (Tomb of Yahya Efendi)
2 CONT * '''Other name''': Tasasız Raziye
2 CONT * '''Religion''': Islam
2 CONT * '''Parents''': Suleiman I and Mahidevran Sultan
2 CONT * '''Children''': Elif Sultan and Safiye Sultan
2 CONT
