1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Updated from [http://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritage-family-trees?itemId=506883-16-2403&action=showRecord&indId=externalindividual-13b58ab81887ec0f350d67441a2bb6dd&mrid=d7c764eb94199502687eff2
2 CONC c607597d9 MyHeritage Match] via son [http://www.geni.com/profile-34664371896 Soloman Hammond] by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 14 2014, 17:10:26 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT One record of interest is the following: 4 September 1798 Montgomery County, Virginia, Deed: Grantor:   JOHN COOPER Grantees: ELIZABETH ROLES HAMMOND, & JOHN COOPER HAMMOND, her son for  Love & affection & other considerations, 65
2 CONC  acres in Mongtomery  County, VirginiaWilliam, John and Edward Elam were among the pioneers  of Southwestern Virginia, however, very little is known about them.   They were amont those who moved on, seeking adventure, or searching
2 CONC   for better locations to establish their homes.
2 CONT
2 CONT 18 August 1788 Israel Christian of Washington Co., NC conveyed 100  acres on Thompson's Creek in Russell County, VA (grate date 2 Oct  1786) to John Elam of Russell County for 40 pounds.
2 CONT
2 CONT 26 May 1794 James and Mary Bush of Russell County conveyed 45 lacres  (grant date to James 15 Dec 1782) to William Elam of Russell County  for 30 poounds.
2 CONT
2 CONT 24 May 1797, Edward Elm obtained 240 acres land grant on Wallens  Creek, Lee County, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT 20 Sept 1798 Edward and wife Jane Elam conveyed 40 acres of the grant  to William Campbell on behalf of his father Col. Arthur Campbell of  Washington Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT 24 Sept 1798 Edward and Jane conveyed 76 acres of the grant lying near  John Own's line to Benjamin Foster.
2 CONT
2 CONT 25 Dec 1798 Edward & Jane Elam conveyed the remaining 130 acres on the  north side of Wallens Ridge to William Ridge.  After that Edward Elam  no longer appears in Lee County records.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deed from JOHN HAMON Senr. and wife MARY to JOHN HAMON, JR. Russell County, Virginia Deed Book 5, Page 13 Executed 10 Dec 1813, Recorded 1814 This Indenture made the tenth day of December in the year of our Lord  one thousand eigh
2 CONC t hundred & thirteen ~ between JOHN HAMON senr. of  Russell County and Commonwealth of Virginia and MARY his wife of the  one part, and JOHN HAMON JR. of the same county of the other part  Witnesseth, That the said JOHN HAMON Seni
2 CONC or and MARY his wife for and  in consideration of the sum of one hundred and five dollars to him in  hand paid, the receipt they do hereby acknowledge have granted  bargained & sold and by these presents do grant bargain and sell 
2 CONC unto  the said John Hamon junr. a certain tract or parcel of land lying and  being in the said county of Russell on both sides of the left hand  fork of Dumps Creek containing thirty acres be the same more or less,  and bounded as
2 CONC  follows; beginning at a buckeye and sugartree neare the  lower forde of the left hand fork of Dumps Creek running up said  branch on the west side on a conditional line to the mouth of the  middle fork thence up sd. branch to the
2 CONC  old patten [sic] line thence  along said line about 7 degrees West to two white oaks in a hollow at  the foot of a ridge S. 45 poles crossing a branch to a hickory and  plumb on the bank of the same N. 62 E. 110 poles crossing be
2 CONC nt [sic]  of sd branch to the beginning, with its appurtanence to have & to hold  the said tract or parcel of land to the said John Hamon junr. his  heirs & assigns forever. And the said John Hamon senr. doth warrant  and forever 
2 CONC defend the said land from the claims of all persons  whatever. In witness whereof the said JOHN HAMON SENR.. and MARY  his  wife have hereunto set their hands and affixed their seals the day and  year first above written. [Signed]
2 CONC  JOHN HAMON  Seal MARY HAMON  Seal Test, Jesse X Fuller Thomas Francis Ambrose Hamon Virginia: At a court held for Russel County the [blank] day of 1814 This Indenture of bargain and sale from John Hamon & Mary his wife to  Jno. H
2 CONC amon jr. was proved by the oaths of Jesse Fuller Thos. Francis &  Ambrose Hamon the witnesses thereto and ordered to be recorded. Teste James P. Carrell D.C. Note: Mary, wife of John Hamon Senior, was the relict of George McCoy.  
2 CONC She and John Hamon Senior had no children of their own.* Reference: [http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=bhreed&id=I36287 RootsWeb's WorldConnect] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: '
