1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Ahmed-Abouelfetouh Mahmoud Fakhry, Bey===
2 CONT "Bey" is a modern Egyptian title of nobility (before the 1953 abolishment of the Nobility) that, depending upon the person holding the title, is comparable to the British titles of Baronet, Knight, Esquire, Honorable, and Gentlema
2 CONC n.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is the 1st grandchild of HM King Fouad I and nephew of HM King Farouk's (though same generation). 
2 CONT He was born in Guiza (Cairo) at the house of his mother the Princess Fewkieh Fouad) house - today Egypt's Senate building - but left Egypt at age 3 following his father's (Mahmoud Fakhry Pasha) nomination as Minister Plenipotentia
2 CONC ry & Envoy Extraordinary (Ambassador) to Paris (France), Brussels (Belgium), Bern (Switzerland), Madrid (Spain), and Lisbon (Portugal) all at the same time (sic!). He studied at Lycée Henri IV, Lycée Jeanson de Sailly, Institut Ra
2 CONC ymond Poincarré, and Institut Polytechnique, Paris, France. Chemical Engineer. He returned to Egypt in 1955 at his father's death. Founder, Proprietor and President of A. Fakhry & Co (1955-1998).
