2 CONT Prince Vasily Vasilyevich Dolgorukov (March 27, 1787 - December 12, 1858[1], St. Petersburg) was a Russian courtier, Jaegermeister, Ober-Stalmeister in the reign of Nicholas I. Vice-President of the Free Economic Society.  He marr
2 CONC ied Princess Varvara Sergeevna Gagarina (1793-31.01.1833).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Vasilyevna (19.04.1814[12]-1869) - baptized (May 07, 1814) in the Court Cathedral of the Winter Palace under the reception of Empress Maria Feodorovna, Freilina, married to the Acting State Councillor Lev Kirillovich Naryshk
2 CONC in (1809-1855), son of Chief Martyr K. A. Naryshkina. According to her contemporary, Maria Vasilyevna had "a wonderful face of rare beauty, a beautiful profile, correct and subtle features, very lively beautiful black eyes and bla
2 CONC ck hair"[13], but also great oddities. She died in insanity, for which she was treated in Paris.
