1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Arkadi Suvorov=
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arkadi_Suvorov '''Arkadi Alexandrovich Suvorov'''], Count of Rymniksky, was a Russian general. A son of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Suvorov '''Alexander Suvorov'''], he rose to the rank 
2 CONC of lieutenant general.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He fought in''' the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Italian_and_Swiss_expedition Italian and Swiss expedition] (1799-1800). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''After his father's''' death Arkadi married [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elena_Aleksandrovna_Naryshkina '''Elena Aleksandrovna Naryshkina'''] (1785-1855 ). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He fought in the''' wars with France in 1807, in Austria in 1809 and in Turkey from 1810 to 1811. He commanded 9th Infantry Division, stationed in the Ukraine, from 1807 onwards. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was killed''' while crossing the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R%C3%A2mnicul_S%C4%83rat Râmnicul Sărat River] on 13 April 1811, though the story stating that he was drowned trying to save his coachman originated with his bi
2 CONC ographer '''E. Fuks''' and is not supported by his memoirs and documentary sources. It is however, supported by [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aleksey_Petrovich_Yermolov '''Aleksey Yermolov''']'s memoirs,as well as by the military
2 CONC  historian Christopher Duffy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He is buried at''' the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Jerusalem_Monastery New Jerusalem Monastery]. He had two daughters - Mary and Barbara - and two sons - [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Arkadyevich_Suvorov '''Al
2 CONC exander'''] and Constantine.
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT <br/>
