2 CONT from wikipedia:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Lvovich_Naryshkin
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Lvovich Naryshkin (Russian: Александр Лвович Нарышкин), born in 1760, died in 1826.
2 CONT
2 CONT Russian noble, he was great chamberlain, chief operating officer of the imperial theatre from 1799 to 1819, Marshal of Nobility of Saint-Petersburg from 1718 to 1726.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Lev Alexandrovich Naryshkin (1733-1799) and brother of Dmitry Lvovich Naryshkin (1764-1838) whose spouse Maria Antonovna Naryshkina (1779-1854) was Alexander I of Russia's mistress. He was a friend of Paul I of Russia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Lvovich Naryshkin and his brother were famous for their great luxury parties which dazzled the Saint-Petersburg nobility.
2 CONT
2 CONT As well as many members of his family, Alexander Lvovich Naryshkin was buried in Alexander Nevsky Lavra.
