2 CONC  Pages (1898, 1st category, in the 44th Dragoon Nizhny Novgorod Regiment). Transferred to the Guard (1913 or 1914) Studied at the Corps of Pages (1893-1898, entered the 5th grade), in the 44th Dragoon Nizhny Novgorod Regiment, adj
2 CONC utant led. Prince Nikolai Mikhailovich (before 09/01/1912 - after 09/01/1913). In exile in France, in 1934 treasurer, secretary and member of the court of honor of the main board of the Union of Pages, by Feb. 1954 Chairman of the
2 CONC  Union of Pages, 1934 General Secretary of the Society of Friends of the "Sentinel", 1939 supported the leader. Prince Vladimir Kirillovich; board member of the Union of Officers of the Caucasian Army in Paris, secretary of the re
2 CONC gimental association of the 17th dragoon regiment, chairman of the Society of Zealots of Russian Military Antiquity. Compositions: Nizhny Novgorod saber // Mollo "Russian edged weapons". Paris, 196?
